@startuml spec-permission-decision
title TaskFlow — Todo Permission Decision (target, exact master table)
skinparam ActivityFontSize 12

start
:Input: todo doc, user_id, profile_id?, is_global_admin?;

if (todo.user_id == user_id?) then (yes)
  :**OWNER**;
  stop
else (no)
endif

if (user in todo.assignees?\n(matches user_id OR profile_id)) then (no)
  partition "visibility fallback" {
    if (visibility == "public") then (yes)
      if (is_global_admin) then (yes)
        :MODERATOR;
        stop
      else (no)
        :VIEWER;
        stop
      endif
    elseif (visibility == "shared") then (yes)
      if (is_global_admin) then (yes)
        :MODERATOR;
        stop
      else (no)
        :no access (None);
        stop
      endif
    else (private)
      :no access (None);
      stop
    endif
  }
else (yes)
  :role = assignee_roles[assignee_id]\n(default **"viewer"** when missing);\nparse case-insensitive:\n"viewer"|anything->VIEWER, "editor"->EDITOR,\n"admin"/"moderator"->MODERATOR;
  stop
endif

note as N1
  Capability matrix (TodoPermission):
  - can_delete_todo ............ OWNER only
  - can_edit_todo_fields ....... MODERATOR, OWNER
  - can_archive_todo ........... OWNER only
  - create/edit/delete task .... EDITOR+ (non-moderators also
    require task.user_id == caller)
  - edit/delete subtask ........ EDITOR+ + creator-match rule
  - create/edit/delete comment . EDITOR+
  - archive task/subtask/comment MODERATOR+

  Task/Subtask extra gate:
  is_owner_or_admin(todo) => always allowed;
  otherwise role EDITOR+ AND creator match.

  transfer_ownership: OWNER only.

  List filters:
  private => {visibility:private, user_id}
  shared  => owner OR assignees in [profile_id,user_id]
  all     => $or of private/shared/public branches
endnote
@enduml
